#
The xtrsyn-functions are for processing the level-3 syntax trees
of ATS3 programs. Note that each processed syntax tree (represented
as a Python data structure) is translated from its original version
in ATS3.
#
Basically, a source program in ATS3 (contained in a text file) is
turned into an internal data structure in Python through a call to
PYDEV_d3parsed_pytrcpy; this data structure is then processed by some
xtrsyn-functions ...
#
